.TH GLANCE 1 "2026" "glance" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glance \- terminal speed reader for files and stdin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glance
[\fIflags\fR] [\fIFILE\fR | \fB\-\fR]
.br
\fICOMMAND\fR |
.B glance
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glance
shows a text one word at a time at a fixed spot, with the letter the eye rests on marked, so it
reads faster than it scrolls. Markdown is read as text: headings, list marks, emphasis and link
targets are left out. Code blocks and tables are shown whole and wait for space.
.PP
Words stay a little longer after a comma or the end of a sentence, and long words longer than
short ones. A pause shows the sentence around the current word.
.PP
When the text comes from a pipe, the keys are read from the terminal, so
\fBpbpaste | glance\fR stays interactive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wpm " " \fIN\fR
Start at \fIN\fR words a minute, from 100 to 1000. Without it, the speed of last time.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-big
Big letters, drawn with a figlet font. Words the font cannot draw are shown plain.
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Start at the beginning, not where this text was left.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-popup
Inside tmux, read in a popup over the current pane. This works without a terminal, as from a tmux
binding or an editor.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help.
.PP
Flags may come before or after the file.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR space ", " enter
Pause and go on. At the end, start over.
.TP
.BR h ", " l " (or left, right)"
A sentence back, a sentence forward. Back first goes to the start of the current sentence.
.TP
.BR j ", " k " (or down, up, \-, +)"
Slower, faster, by 25 words a minute.
.TP
.B f
Big letters on and off.
.TP
.BR q ", " esc
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/glance/settings.json
The speed and the letter size of last time.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/glance/positions.json
Where the last 200 texts were left, by a hash of their content: the same text, from a file or a
pipe, goes on from there. A text read to its end is forgotten.
.PP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME
defaults to
.IR ~/.local/state .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to anything, the focus letter is shown without colour.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glance notes.md
pbpaste | glance
git log \-1 \-\-format=%B | glance
pdftotext paper.pdf \- | glance \-w 450
w3m \-dump https://example.com | glance
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The integrations directory of the source has a tmux configuration, a Vim and Neovim plugin, and
shell helpers for the clipboard, web pages and PDFs:
.UR https://github.com/nyactl/glance
.UE
